 Vinsel\nPortrait by Winni Wintermeyer\n2026\nTool use\nT\nmakes me think he doesn’t see things that \nway. For Brand, maintenance seems to be \na solitary act, profound but more about \npersonal success and fulfillment than tend-\ning to a shared world or making it better.\nB\nCOURTESY OF THE PUBLISHER; WINNI WINTERMEYER/GUARDIAN/EYEVINE/REDUX\nhe handsome new \nbook Maintenance: Of \nEverything, Part One, by \nthe tech industry legend \nStewart Brand, promises \nto be the first in a series \noffering “a comprehen-\nsive overview of the civilizational impor-\ntance of maintenance.” One of Brand’s \nseveral biographers described him as a \nmainstay of both counterculture and cyber-\nculture, and with Maintenance, Brand \nwants us to understand that the upkeep and \nrepair of tools and systems has profound \nimpact on daily life. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1\nDepartment of Mathematics, The University of Pen (https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~kirillov/MATH480-S08/WN.pdf)\nciteturn626search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.7 years ago; \nMath480/540, TOPICS IN MODERN MATH.\nWhat are numbers?\nA.A.Kirillov\nDec. 2007--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMaintece: Part 1 | History books for bookstores - Walmart Business Supplies (https://business.walmart.com/ip/Maintenance-Of-Everything-Maintenance-Of-Everything-Part-One-Book-1-Hardcover-9781953953490/7242466940)\nciteturn626search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; \n\n# Maintenance: Of Everything Maintenance of Everything: Part One, Book 1, (Hardcover)\n\n* * *\n\n## About this item\n\n  * Maintenance: Of Everything Maintenance of Everything: Part One, Book 1, (Hardcover)\n  * Author: Stewart Brand\n  * ISBN: 9781953953490\n  * Format: Hardcover\n  * Publication Date: 2026-01-20\n  * Page Count: 308\n\n\n## At a glance\n\nBook format\n    Hardcover\n\nFiction/nonfiction\n    Non-Fiction\n\nGenr